1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,570
闭上眼，一只蚊子在耳边嗡嗡，
Eyes closed, a mosquito buzzes by your ear,

2
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:04,630
你一巴掌就知道往左边拍。
and you know to slap left.

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,010
耳朵又没长眼睛，
Your ears have no eyes.

4
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:08,030
它怎么知道声音从哪来？
So how do they know where a sound comes from?

5
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:11,610
即将开幕的进博会上，一款人工耳蜗要来首秀，
At the upcoming China Import Expo, a cochlear implant debuts,

6
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:14,120
卖点就是：能找出声音的方向。
and its selling point is finding where sound comes from.

7
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,570
它叫INTEGRO，
It's called Integro,

8
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:17,440
据报道用AI来处理声音。
and it reportedly uses AI to process sound.

9
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,760
今天的烧脑问题：
Today's brain teaser:

10
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:21,200
两只耳朵，怎么算出一个方向？
how do two ears work out a direction?

11
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,260
先看你的脑袋：两只耳朵，
Look at your head: two ears,

12
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:25,610
一左一右，中间隔着一颗头。
one left, one right, a head in between.

13
00:00:25,610 --> 00:00:28,220
蚊子在左边，声音先到左耳，
Mosquito on the left: the sound hits your left ear first,

14
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:30,550
再绕过脑袋，才到右耳。
then wraps around your head to the right.

15
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,540
声音一秒钟走三百四十米，
Sound travels 340 meters a second,

16
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,980
绕过脑袋，估算大约二十厘米。
and the trip around your head is roughly 20 centimeters.

17
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,640
算一下：两只耳朵最多
Do the math: the two ears differ by at most

18
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,090
只差零点六毫秒。
0.6 milliseconds.

19
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:40,010
眨一下眼要一百多毫秒，
A blink takes over 100 milliseconds.

20
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,050
这个差比眨眼短几百倍。
This gap is hundreds of times shorter.

21
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:44,450
可你的大脑，最灵的时候能分出
Yet at its best your brain can tell apart

22
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:46,120
大约十微秒的差别！
about ten microseconds!

23
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,040
怎么做到的？想象两个人
How? Picture two runners

24
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,070
从两头往中间跑着送信。
carrying letters from both ends toward the middle.

25
00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:53,720
左耳的信先出发，两人就在偏右的地方碰头；
The left letter leaves first, so they meet right of center.

26
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,400
大脑看在哪碰头，就知道方向。
Where they meet tells the brain the direction.

27
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,980
这叫“延迟线”模型，
It's called the delay-line model,

28
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:00,950
在猫头鹰的脑子里真找到了这样的线路。
and barn owls really have wiring like this.

29
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:02,730
反转一：光靠时间差，
Twist one: timing alone

30
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:04,450
遇到高音就犯迷糊。
gets confused by high notes.

31
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:07,000
高音的波很短，脑袋就像一堵墙，
High notes have short waves, so your head acts like a wall

32
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,160
挡出一片“声音的影子”。
and casts a sound shadow.

33
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:11,050
所以离得远的那只耳朵，
So the far ear

34
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:12,550
听到的声音更小。
hears it quieter.

35
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:15,080
低音看时间差，高音看音量差，
Low notes: timing. High notes: loudness.

36
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:16,650
大脑两样一起用。
The brain uses both.

37
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:18,340
反转二，最反直觉：
Twist two, the weird one:

38
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:21,470
正前方和正后方，时间差一模一样！
dead ahead and dead behind give the exact same timing!

39
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:23,040
前面和后面的声音，
A sound in front and one behind

40
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,740
到两只耳朵一样远。
are equally far from both ears.

41
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:25,920
这时候靠耳廓，
Now your outer ear takes over,

42
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:28,230
就是你耳朵上那些弯弯绕绕。
all those curls and folds.

43
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:31,710
声音从不同方向进来，被弯弯绕绕弹一弹，
Sound from each direction bounces off the folds,

44
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:33,300
音色就悄悄变了。
and its tone quietly changes.

45
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,870
大脑从小就记住了：
Your brain learned long ago:

46
00:01:34,870 --> 00:01:36,900
这种音色，就是在后面。
this tone means behind you.

47
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,950
还拿不准？你会下意识地
Still not sure? You tilt your head

48
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:40,000
歪一下头。
without thinking.

49
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,850
头一歪，时间差就变了，
Tilt, and the timing changes.

50
00:01:41,850 --> 00:01:43,150
答案马上出来。
Answer found.

51
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:46,740
想帮人找方向的设备，也得用好几个麦克风，
A device that helps people find direction needs several microphones

52
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,470
把这笔账再算一遍。
to do the same math again.

53
00:01:48,470 --> 00:01:49,710
机器人也一样：
Robots do it too:

54
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:52,140
扫地机、机器狗、智能音箱。
robot vacuums, robot dogs, smart speakers.

55
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:54,260
智能音箱上有一圈麦克风，
A smart speaker has a ring of microphones,

56
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,980
比的就是谁先听到。
comparing who hears it first.

57
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:57,480
麦克风隔得越远，
The farther apart the microphones,

58
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:58,910
方向算得越准。
the sharper the direction.

59
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,970
友情提示：听得出方向，
Fine print: hearing the direction

60
00:02:00,970 --> 00:02:02,590
不等于听得清楚。
is not the same as hearing clearly.

61
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:04,150
这款耳蜗好不好用，
How well this implant works

62
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:06,180
还要看真实使用的数据。
still depends on real-world data.

63
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,320
所以两只耳朵怎么算方向？
So how do two ears find a direction?

64
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:11,470
比时间、比音量、听音色、再歪个头。
Timing, loudness, tone, and a head tilt.

65
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:13,200
一套微秒级的算法，
A microsecond-level algorithm

66
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,860
天天在你头上跑。
running on your head all day.

67
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,750
可惜，算出蚊子在左边，
Sadly, knowing the mosquito is on the left

68
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:18,240
不代表你拍得着。
doesn't mean you'll hit it.

69
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,030
它早飞了，
It's long gone,

70
00:02:19,030 --> 00:02:21,100
还顺手在右边叮了一口。
and it bit your right side on the way out.

